  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given that the minor of ${m}_{21}$ is $11$, find all the possible values of $y$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}y & \\frac{3}{2} & y \\\\ 25 & 4-y & 12y \\\\ y & 2 & -6y\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we remove the second row and first column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & \\frac{3}{2} & y \\\\ 25 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & 2 & -6y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${m}_{21}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & y \\\\ 2 & -6y\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & y \\\\ 2 & -6y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-6y)-y\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-11y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${m}_{21}$ is $11$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-11y & =11 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=-1.$",
